Here's the full audit of the Printify API integration:

Printify API Audit
Authentication & Configuration
Token: PRINTIFY_API_TOKEN — stored in .env.local and as a Supabase Edge Function secret (Deno.env.get("PRINTIFY_API_TOKEN"))

Shop ID: stored in the settings table (printify_shop_id column) — configurable via Admin → Settings UI

Base URL: https://api.printify.com/v1

Token scopes (decoded from JWT): shops.manage, shops.read, catalog.read, orders.read, orders.write, products.read, products.write, webhooks.read, webhooks.write, uploads.read, uploads.write, print_providers.read, user.info

⚠️ The PRINTIFY_API_TOKEN in .env.local is a live JWT token exposed in the file. It should be rotated and stored only as a Supabase secret, not in .env.local.

Architecture
All Printify API calls are proxied through a Supabase Edge Function at supabase/functions/printify-proxy/index.ts. The Next.js frontend never calls Printify directly — it calls the proxy via ${SUPABASE_URL}/functions/v1/printify-proxy/....

Proxy Endpoints
Method	Path	Printify API Call
GET	/shops	GET /shops.json
GET	/products?shop_id=	GET /shops/{id}/products.json
GET	/products/:id?shop_id=	GET /shops/{id}/products/{id}.json
POST	/products?shop_id=	POST /shops/{id}/products.json
PUT	/products/:id?shop_id=	PUT /shops/{id}/products/{id}.json
DELETE	/products/:id?shop_id=	DELETE /shops/{id}/products/{id}.json
POST	/orders?shop_id=	POST /shops/{id}/orders.json
GET	/orders/:id?shop_id=	GET /shops/{id}/orders/{id}.json
GET	/shipping?shop_id=	GET /shops/{id}/shipping/options.json
POST	/shipping?shop_id=	POST /shops/{id}/shipping/calculations.json
GET	/blueprints	GET /catalog/blueprints.json
GET	/blueprints/:id/providers	GET /catalog/blueprints/{id}/print_providers.json
GET	/blueprints/:id/providers/:pid/variants	GET /catalog/blueprints/{id}/print_providers/{pid}/variants.json
GET	/blueprints/:id/providers/:pid/shipping	GET /catalog/blueprints/{id}/print_providers/{pid}/shipping.json
POST	/sync?shop_id=	Full sync — fetches all products + shipping profiles, upserts to products table
Where Printify Is Used
admin/products/page.tsx — "Sync Printify" button calls POST /sync, reads printify_shop_id from settings

admin/settings/page.tsx — UI to set printify_shop_id, shows printify_connected status badge

admin/orders/page.tsx — displays printify_order_id on orders

supabase/functions/stripe-webhook/index.ts — on successful Stripe payment, directly calls https://api.printify.com/v1/shops/{id}/orders.json (bypasses the proxy) using PRINTIFY_API_TOKEN + PRINTIFY_SHOP_ID env vars

src/lib/supabase.ts — getShippingQuote() reads cached shipping_info from the products table (populated during sync, no live Printify call)

src/app/api/shipping-diagnostic/route.ts — reads printify_connected and printify_shop_id from settings for diagnostics

Database Fields
products.printify_id — Printify product ID

products.blueprint_id / print_provider_id — blueprint/provider reference

products.shipping_info — cached shipping profile (JSON, populated at sync time)

products.content_locked — prevents Printify re-sync from overwriting curated title/description/image

settings.printify_shop_id — the connected shop ID

settings.printify_connected — boolean flag set to true after a successful sync

orders.printify_order_id — Printify order ID after fulfillment submission

Key Issues to Note
Live token in .env.local — the JWT is committed/present in the file. Should only live as a Supabase secret.

Stripe webhook bypasses the proxy — it calls Printify directly rather than going through printify-proxy, creating two code paths for order submission.

No shop ID in .env.local — PRINTIFY_SHOP_ID env var is only a fallback in the webhook; the primary source is the DB settings table. If the DB is empty, orders won't be submitted.

Single shop only — the entire system is hardcoded to one printify_shop_id from settings. No multi-shop support.

