What a Printify webhook would do
Printify webhooks notify you when things happen on their end — e.g. order:shipped, order:fulfilled, product:updated. You'd use them to automatically update order tracking/fulfillment status in your DB without polling.

Does this app need one?
No, not right now. Here's why:

Order fulfillment flow is push-only: Stripe webhook (stripe-webhook/index.ts) fires on checkout.session.completed, submits the order directly to Printify (POST /shops/{id}/orders.json), and saves the printify_order_id back to the DB. That's the entire loop.

No tracking updates — the app never shows customers a tracking number or shipment status, so there's nothing to receive back from Printify.

No product sync automation — product sync is manual (admin clicks "Sync Printify"), not event-driven.

When you would need a Printify webhook
Event	Use case
order:shipment:created	Auto-update fulfillment_status + tracking number in DB, trigger shipping email to customer
order:fulfilled	Mark order complete
product:updated	Auto re-sync a product when it changes in Printify
If you want to add shipping notification emails to customers, that's when you'd register a webhook pointing at a new Supabase edge function like supabase/functions/printify-webhook/index.ts. Want me to build that?

