what is Blueprint


Context
In Printify, a Blueprint is the base product template — it defines the physical product type.

Examples:

Blueprint 12 = Unisex Heavy Cotton Tee (Gildan 5000)

Blueprint 77 = Unisex Hoodie (Gildan 18500)

Blueprint 200 = Ceramic Mug 11oz

Think of it as the product mold. It defines:

What the product is (t-shirt, hoodie, mug, hat)

Available sizes and colors

Print areas (front, back, sleeve)

Which print providers can fulfill it

How it fits in this app
When a product is synced from Printify, the DB stores:

Field	Example	Purpose
blueprint_id	"12"	What type of product it is
print_provider_id	"99"	Which printer fulfills it (e.g. Monster Digital)
shipping_info	{profiles:[...]}	Cached shipping rates for that blueprint+provider combo
The blueprint_id + print_provider_id pair is used during sync to fetch and cache the shipping profile — so checkout can calculate shipping costs without a live Printify API call.

In plain terms
Blueprint = the blank product (e.g. "Gildan tee")
Your design + blueprint = a Printify product
Blueprint + print provider = who makes it and how much to ship it

