Here's what changed and why:

The missing piece — the publish handshake:

Printify's custom integration flow is a 3-step handshake:

You click "Publish" in Printify → Printify fires product:publish:started to your webhook

Your webhook receives it, saves the product to your DB

Your webhook must call back POST /shops/{id}/products/{id}/publishing_succeeded.json → Printify marks it "Published"

Without step 3, Printify waits indefinitely and shows "Publishing...".

The callback also sends publishing_failed.json if anything goes wrong, so Printify shows a proper error instead of hanging.

After deploying, go into Printify and try publishing one of the stuck products again — it should flip to "Published" within seconds.

